# Captured browser session state. `tests/e2e/.auth/participant.json` holds a
# live `zugzwang_session` cookie; it is untracked but was NOT ignored, so a
# single `git add -A` would have committed a working session token to a repo
# whose history cannot be rewritten. Ignored here rather than deleted — the
# files are somebody's working state and are not this PR's to remove.
# ⚠ Nothing in this repository creates them: no Playwright, no
# `playwright.config.*`, no `storageState` caller (AGENTS.md §1/§9). Whatever
# wrote them ran out of band, and that is flagged separately — the ignore stops
# the leak, it does not explain the origin.
tests/e2e/.auth/

