# Harness-created git worktrees nested INSIDE the repo. Git already skips them
# via `.git/info/exclude`, but that file is per-clone and un-committed, and
# Biome reads `.gitignore` (`vcs.useIgnoreFile`), not git's exclude chain — so a
# nested worktree carries its own `biome.json` into `biome check .`, which then
# refuses with "Found a nested root configuration". That breaks `just verify`
# AND the lefthook pre-push hook for every session in the tree, which is a gate
# that fails closed on an artifact of the tooling rather than on the code.
.claude/worktrees/

